one identified benefit offer by a distributor to a client in the SFC-authorised-fund setting.","A meaningful product association created by the manner of offering can suffice without product-specific gift eligibility.","Actual investor distraction is not a separate factual prerequisite; the stated purpose informs the linkage interpretation.","Gift and discount classifications are supplied judgments. The result flags only this selected control."],"citations":[{"quote":"The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"other than a discount of fees or charges","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"Reaches a meaningful association produced by campaign presentation as well as an express connection. In the account-opening-gift example in R1, contextual linkage to one fund house flags the non-discount gift even though eligibility is investment-neutral. This reading has stronger support in 'offered in such a way' and the distraction rationale, but the missing FAQ prevents settling how much contextual association suffices.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed offer is by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds to a client in that distribution setting.","name":"distributor_client_setting","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to the client and qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer expressly promotes, or its eligibility terms directly connect it to, a specific investment product or a particular product type, including funds from a particular fund house.","name":"direct_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The manner or campaign context of offering the gift meaningfully associates it with a specific investment product or particular product type, independently of an express promotion or eligibility connection.","name":"contextual_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and gift_offered (not fee_discount) (or direct_product_nexus contextual_product_nexus))","result_type":"bool","scope":"distributor_client_setting"},"local_id":"gift_contextual_nexus","questions":["What distinguishes a meaningful contextual product association from incidental placement alongside fund advertising under the missing FAQ?"],"statement":"Read 'offered in such a way that they are linked' as extending the control to indirect but meaningful promotional associations created by presentation or campaign design. A non-discount gift linked in that manner to a product or fund-house category falls within the selected control even when its eligibility terms are product-neutral. The fee-discount exception continues to apply.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: contextual product connection"}]}},"run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027"}